	quest.702B45B36975C275.quest_desc: [
		"Hey, do you know about &5&nChromatic Compound&r? It was once a hidden item in the &2&nCreate&r mod, and we designed an interesting &bautomation puzzle&r for you to obtain this unique material."
		""
		"{image:createcasing:item/chorium_ingot width:16 height:16 align:center}"
		""
		"Put simply, you first need to craft some &d&nChorium Ingots&r as the raw material. Then dye them using a &2Mechanical Mixer&r (&4consumes dye&r) or &6Beam Focusing&r (&3does not consume dye&r). One &d&nChorium Ingot&r can be dyed with 2 different colors. When thrown into water, if the 2 colors are the correct pair, it produces a &b&nAttuned Chorium Ingot&r; otherwise it fades back into a &d&nChorium Ingot&r."
		""
		"{image:kubejs:item/chorium_attuned width:16 height:16 align:center}"
		""
		"The correct color pair is refreshed every time a &2recipe completes&r, but you are allowed to throw in more than one ingot at a time; this counts as completing it once. Finally, &b&nAttuned Chorium Ingots&r can be infused with &aFluid Uranium&r to become &5&nChromatic Compound&r."
		""
		"Using the &2Round Robin&r mode of a &eBrass Tunnel&r is a good automation option; you only need to set up &6dyeing in 6 colors and let the production line loop&r."
	]
	quest.702B45B36975C275.quest_subtitle: "The Colors of Randomness"
